## Build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
publish/
*.binlog

## Repo-local NuGet feed: its CONTENT is produced by building build/BHS.Revit.Sdk and never
## committed, but the directory itself is. NuGet.config names it as a package source, and NuGet
## refuses a source that does not exist - NU1301, on the very first restore, before anything can
## create it. So a fresh clone did not build at all, including the bootstrap step CLAUDE.md tells
## you to run first. Found by CI on its first run, which is exactly what CI is for: the directory
## had existed on this machine for months.
## A nested artifacts/ anywhere is build output, ignored as it always was. Spelled out because
## the root exception below is anchored: writing `artifacts/*` alone quietly stopped ignoring
## every other artifacts directory in the tree, which the old unanchored `artifacts/` had covered.
**/artifacts/
!/artifacts/

## The root feed: the directory is tracked, its content never.
/artifacts/*
!/artifacts/feed/
/artifacts/feed/*
!/artifacts/feed/.gitkeep

