# Empty Revit models used by the launch and document checks. Kept out of git on purpose: about
# 6 MB each, opaque, and rewritten wholesale whenever Revit touches them - four more copies in
# history on every re-save. Recreate them from Revit, one per supported release.
/testdata/*.rvt

## Other assistants' local configuration. Ignored rather than committed, by the owner's decision -
## unlike .claude/agents, which is tracked because those definitions are shared.
##
## Not cosmetic: the sweep's record refuses to claim a clean tree, and `git status` counts
## untracked files as dirty. It is right to - a stray .cs anywhere under source/ would be compiled
## into what the sweep then measures - so anything living in the tree and belonging to nobody's
## build has to be named here, or no record can ever be taken again.
/AGENTS.md
/.codex/
